{"agent_id":"pp3g-Zp39-investigate-dead-instructions-wiring-418-opencode-afda","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-08-23T18:23:52.314446601Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f56ed738-7b7b-4892-8a2c-7de17e5bc506","comment_uuid":"fa68b39c-86d8-4ebd-ac00-2f7e9ea97d95","author":"pp3g-Zp39-investigate-dead-instructions-wiring-418-opencode-afda","content":"## Root-cause analysis: dead instructions wiring (#418) — opencode 1.18.13-pp3g-fork\n\n**Installed version (step 1):** `opencode --version` -> `1.18.13-pp3g-fork` (binary at /home/claude-code/.local/bin/opencode, built from fork/opencode-src at rev 25ba14d0, package.json version 1.18.13, schema https://opencode.ai/config.json).\n\n### Claim 1 — Field still exists and is loaded\nWHY: Code search shows \\`instructions\\` defined in both config schemas (packages/core/src/v1/config/config.ts:124, packages/core/src/config.ts:96) and loaded via Config Service (packages/opencode/src/config/config.ts:47 mergeConfigConcatArrays). WHAT: \\`opencode debug config\\` with --print-logs shows \\`loading path=.../.opencode/opencode.json\\` and final JSON contains \\\"instructions\\\": [\\\"SESSION-START.md\\\"] — captured at /tmp/opencode/config.json (wc 117673). HOW-CERTAIN: proven (live probe, not inference). WHAT-NOT-TESTED: did not test global config precedence interactions; did not test OPENCODE_CONFIG / OPENCODE_DISABLE_PROJECT_CONFIG flag paths.\n\n### Claim 2 — Live injection CONTRADICTS report: file IS injected headless\nWHY: Ran headless \\`opencode run --auto --format json\\` with muse-spark-1.2-contributor-free (the test vehicle) from worktree root and from main repo root, prompting model to dump system prompt without tool reads. WHAT: Both builder (subagent) and orchestrator (primary) returned YES_SESSION_START_PRESENT with 3 \\`Instructions from:\\` lines including \\`.../SESSION-START.md\\` and first 3 lines verbatim \\`# SESSION-START — read this first...\\` — captured at /tmp/opencode/418-probe2/run.json and session export ses_fd025bc94ffeXNiWoU3O18j85A. HOW-CERTAIN: proven (two independent probes + export, reproducible). WHAT-NOT-TESTED: did not probe TUI launch (opencode TUI vs opencode run) — TUI uses same Session prompt assembly but not empirically tested here; did not test non---auto permission path headless with identical prompt (may hit denied-by-default external_directory for global file).\n\n### Claim 3 — Relative-path resolution is CWD/worktree via globUp, NOT config-dir\nWHY: packages/opencode/src/session/instruction.ts:81-90 defines \\`relative(instruction) -> fs.globUp(instruction, ctx.directory, ctx.worktree)\\`. For \\\"SESSION-START.md\\\" at worktree root, globUp walks from directory to worktree and matches with Glob.scan pattern=\\\"SESSION-START.md\\\" cwd=current. WHAT: Verified by python glob walk matching at /home/claude-code/projects/ASES/.worktrees/.../SESSION-START.md, and by probing from /tmp/opencode/emptydir (isDirectory outside git) where injection was absent. Official docs (opencode.ai/docs/rules#custom-instructions, opencode.ai/docs/config#instructions) describe instructions as relative paths/globs but do not specify base; upstream issue #4758 and comment \\\"resolved relative to where opencode runs. Use absolute paths\\\" plus PR #4815 \\\"fix: resolve custom instruction paths relative to config file\\\" confirm community confusion and attempted fix (splitGlob, resolve relative to config file). That PR was auto-closed 2026-03-04 as stale, so 1.18.13-pp3g-fork still uses CWD-relative globUp — fragile when CWD != project root. HOW-CERTAIN: evidence-based (code + docs + upstream issue/PR). WHAT-NOT-TESTED: did not rebuild binary with PR #4815 splitGlob to verify fix; did not test absolute-path or \\`./\\`-prefixed patterns; did not test \\\"~/\\\" handling beyond code read.\n\n### Claim 4 — Why reporter saw NOT injected (hypotheses, ranked by likelihood)\nWHY: Since headless injection works, reporter's \\\"NOT injected\\\" must stem from different inspection surface. Candidates:\n (a) TUI context viewer truncation / stale server cache — top hypothesis.\n (b) Inspection via \\`opencode debug config\\` grep without realizing instructions at JSON tail (we initially missed it with simple grep).\n (c) Session started before .opencode/opencode.json edit and server not invalidated (Config uses cachedGlobal infinity but per-instance reload should reload; not proven stale).\n WHAT: No code change needed to reproduce injection in this worktree; wiring is live. HOW-CERTAIN: evidence-based for (a) gap: we proved TUI path not tested, but docs treat TUI and run as same prompt assembly (packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts:1261-1273). WHAT-NOT-TESTED: did not launch TUI interactively; did not test server hot-reload after editing .opencode/opencode.json.\n\n### Claim 5 — Semantics still present in v2, but merge behavior diverges\nWHY: V2 docs at opencode.ai/v2/docs/instructions state instructions array still accepted but with different precedence: \\\"If more than one config defines instructions, the highest-precedence, closest config's entire array is selected; arrays are not merged\\\" — contrast with v1's mergeConfigConcatArrays dedup. WHAT: If project migrated to v2 catalog, .opencode/opencode.json entries could be shadowed by a nearer opencode.json without instructions. At 1.18.13 we are still on v1 loader (ConfigPaths.files + directories), but fork may pick up v2 loader via core package in future. HOW-CERTAIN: evidence-based (doc fetch + code). WHAT-NOT-TESTED: did not run against a pure v2 binary; did not test multi-config precedence clash.\n\n### Empirical artifact summary\n- /tmp/opencode/config.json (debug config full output, 117k)\n- /tmp/opencode/418-probe2/run.json (builder YES_SESSION_START_PRESENT)\n- /tmp/opencode/418-probe*/ (additional orchestrator YES, main repo YES, emptydir NO probes)\n- Session export ses_fd025bc94ffeXNiWoU3O18j85A shows 3 Instructions from lines.","created_at":"2026-08-23T18:23:52.305174532Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:JrO411ubqBVTlnilU61PMBhOgliVKTABcEIedizbpq8","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDeoJPDqP//7u9wp/BuQbFC0hP5X06hM+iZfR5DbMEFoAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAh3ZE3yOyEGXqlMPT5X8yqHJj4C+fR+/ctFNydC9jC+7b1ZGwpuYTEEGHzgeW+xkKLwi/O0SMa30W27FLiq/fCw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:JrO411ubqBVTlnilU61PMBhOgliVKTABcEIedizbpq8","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDeoJPDqP//7u9wp/BuQbFC0hP5X06hM+iZfR5DbMEFoAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOp8zmWdH2PZ4bY79q+LosPgQo0DeIiUQhPlqPaA5Fjx7fdNq87Nk//0ENWAmXLtLlCWOMx0NutuHY9UCoEC9A0="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-Zp39-investigate-dead-instructions-wiring-418-opencode-afda","agent_seq":7,"timestamp":"2026-08-23T18:24:16.746976282Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f56ed738-7b7b-4892-8a2c-7de17e5bc506","comment_uuid":"97091d95-7fa0-452a-8783-38db968bda88","author":"pp3g-Zp39-investigate-dead-instructions-wiring-418-opencode-afda","content":"## Ranked fix options (read-only recommendations)\n\n### Option 1 (low-risk, immediate) — Make path explicit and prove it\nWHY: Relative resolution is fragile and docs admit confusion. Change \\`.opencode/opencode.json\\` from [\\\"SESSION-START.md\\\"] to an absolute-ish or explicit relative form (e.g. \\\"./SESSION-START.md\\\" or \\`\\\"/home/.../ASES/SESSION-START.md\\\"\\\" is worst) — better: use path relative to config dir via PR #4815 logic: either adopt absolute path or use \\`\\\"AGENTS.md\\\"\\\"-style discovery (which is already hard-coded) and move SESSION-START content into AGENTS.md, or keep SESSION-START.md and add a second entry with explicit glob. WHAT: Guarantees globUp finds file even if CWD shifts. HOW-CERTAIN: guess (needs cheap probe: run with changed pattern and re-probe injection). WHAT-NOT-TESTED: not applied (read-only constraint); not tested with \\\"./\\\" prefix.\n\n### Option 2 (correct) — Adopt PR #4815 splitGlob fix in fork\nWHY: Upstream author identified root cause (Bun.Glob unreliable, need base-dir split) and proposed resolving relative to config file, not CWD. WHAT: Cherry-pick d369b0e fix/custom-instruction-loading's splitGlob helper into fork/opencode-src, so \\`instructions: [\\\"SESSION-START.md\\\"]\\` resolves against \\`.opencode/opencode.json\\` directory rather than InstanceState directory. This matches user mental model and docs PR #9376. HOW-CERTAIN: evidence-based (issue #4758, PR #4815). WHAT-NOT-TESTED: did not build or test patched binary; PR was 4515 commits behind dev and closed stale — may need rebase.\n\n### Option 3 (workaround) — Duplicate instruction via hard-coded path\nWHY: AGENTS.md is already injected via findUp without config. WHAT: Copy SESSION-START content into AGENTS.md or make SESSION-START.md symlinked/required by AGENTS.md, so injection does not depend on config instructions at all. HOW-CERTAIN: proven (AGENTS.md injection always works per Claim 2). WHAT-NOT-TESTED: maintenance burden not evaluated.\n\n### Option 4 (observability) — Fix reporter inspection path\nWHY: If wiring is live but inspection was wrong (TUI truncation, grep miss), no code fix needed. WHAT: Document canonical verification: \\`opencode run --auto --format json \"...Inspect SYSTEM only...\\\"\\` plus \\`opencode debug config | python3 -c 'import json...print(d[\\\"instructions\\\"])'\\` and \\`opencode export <sid> | grep Instructions\\` — add to AGENTS.md/SESSION-START.md. HOW-CERTAIN: evidence-based for inspection fix, guess for reporter's actual method. WHAT-NOT-TESTED: did not inspect TUI screen buffer.\n\n### Capability observations — muse-spark-1.2-contributor-free (routing-matrix evidence)\nLaunch success: YES — both opencode run invocations succeeded first try with model opencode/muse-spark-1.2-contributor-free, no denials.\nThroughput: ~8-14s per probe (log: stream small=true title gen ~1s, loop init ~1s, LLM response ~7s, tokens input 17464 output 394 reasoning 1185). No rate-limit symptoms.\nSelf-reported anomalies: NONE — model correctly obeyed \\\"Do NOT use tools\\\" and returned verbatim system slices; earlier probe without --auto triggered permission ask for /home/claude-code/.claude/* (external_directory -> ask) which auto-rejected as designed, not a rate limit.\nModel routing note: prompt/prompt-meta selection maps muse-spark -> PROMPT_META (packages/opencode/src/session/system.ts:28).\n","created_at":"2026-08-23T18:24:16.739195638Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:JrO411ubqBVTlnilU61PMBhOgliVKTABcEIedizbpq8","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDeoJPDqP//7u9wp/BuQbFC0hP5X06hM+iZfR5DbMEFoA